        "path": "/Users/marcin/Documents/VIMSS/ontology/Mechs/MediaIngredientMech/.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/queue/preliminary-v5/inputs/culturemech/data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/middlebrook_7h10_agar_with_oadc_enrichment.yaml",
        "sha256": "6f333ed2123da2eff1755433d881cb48686a58dca10daaa0fc3da07b296e9f1a",
        "text": "id: CultureMech:002743\nname: middlebrook_7h10_agar_with_oadc_enrichment\noriginal_name: MIDDLEBROOK 7H10 AGAR WITH OADC ENRICHMENT\ncategory: bacterial\nmedium_type: COMPLEX\ncomposition_type: UNDEFINED\nphysical_state: SOLID_AGAR\nmedia_term:\n  preferred_term: JCM Medium J386\n  term:\n    id: mediadive.medium:J386\n    label: MIDDLEBROOK 7H10 AGAR WITH OADC ENRICHMENT\nnotes: 'Source: JCM Medium 386 | Link: https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=386\n\n\n  The JCM Middlebrook 7H10 Agar with OADC Enrichment table lists Middlebrook 7H10\n  agar, glycerol, distilled water, and a 100 ml/L aseptic addition of Middlebrook\n  OADC Enrichment.'\ningredients:\n- preferred_term: Middlebrook 7H10 agar (BD-Difco)\n  concentration:\n    value: '19'\n    unit: G_PER_L\n  notes: JCM Medium 386 lists this commercial BD-Difco medium base as supplied.\n- preferred_term: Glycerol\n  concentration:\n    value: '5'\n    unit: ML_PER_L\n  term:\n    id: CHEBI:17754\n    label: glycerol\n  mediaingredientmech_chebi_term:\n    id: CHEBI:17754\n    label: glycerol\n  notes: JCM Medium 386 lists glycerol as 5 ml/L.\n- preferred_term: Distilled water\n  concentration:\n    value: '895'\n    unit: ML_PER_L\n  term:\n    id: CHEBI:15377\n    label: water\n  mediaingredientmech_chebi_term:\n    id: CHEBI:15377\n    label: water\n  notes: JCM Medium 386 uses 895 ml/L distilled water before OADC addition.\n- preferred_term: Middlebrook OADC Enrichment (BD-BBL)\n  concentration:\n    value: '100'\n    unit: ML_PER_L\n  notes: JCM Medium 386 aseptically adds this commercial BD-BBL enrichment.\npreparation_steps:\n- step_number: 1\n  action: AUTOCLAVE\n  description: Sterilize the Middlebrook 7H10 agar, glycerol, and distilled water\n    at 121 C for 10 min.\n- step_number: 2\n  action: COOL\n  description: Cool to 50-55 C.\n- step_number: 3\n  action: MIX\n  description: Aseptically add 100 ml/L Middlebrook OADC Enrichment (BD-BBL) and mix\n    thoroughly.\napplications:\n- Microbial cultivation\ncuration_history:\n- timestamp: '2026-01-26T17:53:16.472084Z'\n  curator: mediadive-import\n  action: Imported from MediaDive\n  notes: 'Source: JCM, ID: J386'\n- timestamp: '2026-03-13T06:19:15.424569Z'\n  curator: culturemech-id-assigner-v1.0\n  action: Assigned CultureMech ID\n  notes: 'Assigned stable identifier: CultureMech:002743'\n- timestamp: '2026-03-17T06:30:02.000000Z'\n  curator: mediaingredientmech-enrichment-v1.0\n  action: Added MediaIngredientMech links\n  notes: Linked ingredients to MediaIngredientMech identifiers\n- timestamp: '2026-03-17T19:45:28.820479+00:00'\n  curator: normalize_media_names_to_snake_case.py\n  action: NAME_NORMALIZED\n  notes: Normalized name from \"MIDDLEBROOK 7H10 AGAR WITH OADC ENRICHMENT\" to \"middlebrook_7h10_agar_with_oadc_enrichment\"\n    for consistent matching\n- timestamp: '2026-06-05T07:41:33.901166+00:00'\n  curator: mim-legacy-to-chebi-migration-v1.0\n  action: Refreshed legacy MediaIngredientMech links to CHEBI keying\n  notes: 'Replaced 2 legacy mediaingredientmech_term link(s) with mediaingredientmech_chebi_term\n    (id-safe: ingredient''s own CHEBI + label). MIM deprecated the MediaIngredientMech:NNNNNN\n    id scheme.'\n- timestamp: '2026-09-10T00:00:00-07:00'\n  curator: repair_jcm_middlebrook_hemin_score20.py\n  action: RESOLVED_JCM_MIDDLEBROOK_HEMIN_SCORE20\n  changes: Resolved JCM Medium 386/714 Middlebrook-hemin composition\n  source: https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=386\n  notes: Rebuilt the recipe from live JCM Medium 386 and 714 pages.\nvariant_children:\n- path: data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/JCM_J714_HEMIN_MEDIUM_FOR_MYCOBACTERIUM.yaml\n  relationship: SUPPLEMENTED_VARIANT\n  id: CultureMech:003061\n  name: hemin_medium_for_mycobacterium\n  notes: Adds 60 micromol/L hemin solubilized with 1 N NaOH.\ndata_quality_flags:\n- ingredients_curated\n- has_ontology_mappings\n- has_unmapped_ingredients\nreferences:\n- reference: https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=386\n"
      }
