ption: Adjust pH if specified in original formulation\n- step_number: 3\n  action: FILTER_STERILIZE\n  description: Sterilize by filtration (0.22 μm) to preserve heat-sensitive components\ncuration_history:\n- timestamp: '2026-01-27T07:21:42.809402Z'\n  curator: mediadb-import\n  action: Imported from MediaDB\n  notes: 'Source: MediaDB (Institute for Systems Biology), Medium ID: 33, Reference:\n    Mazumdar et al. (2014) PLOS One'\n- timestamp: '2026-01-28T19:48:21.045290Z'\n  curator: chebi-enrichment\n  action: Added CHEBI ontology terms to ingredients\n  notes: Enriched using MicrobeMediaParam and MediaDive chemical mappings\n- timestamp: '2026-02-06T05:10:29.348397Z'\n  curator: invalid-chebi-removal\n  action: Removed 1 invalid CHEBI ID(s)\n  notes: Removed CHEBI IDs with invalid format (7+ digits) from MicrobeMediaParam\n    source data\n- timestamp: '2026-03-13T06:19:47.116813Z'\n  curator: culturemech-id-assigner-v1.0\n  action: Assigned CultureMech ID\n  notes: 'Assigned stable identifier: CultureMech:007240'\n- timestamp: '2026-03-17T06:30:10.000000Z'\n  curator: mediaingredientmech-enrichment-v1.0\n  action: Added MediaIngredientMech links\n  notes: Linked ingredients to MediaIngredientMech identifiers\n- timestamp: '2026-03-17T19:46:05.311201+00:00'\n  curator: normalize_media_names_to_snake_case.py\n  action: NAME_NORMALIZED\n  notes: Normalized name from \"CDM/LP\" to \"cdm_lp\" for consistent matching\n- timestamp: '2026-06-05T07:40:52.804984+00:00'\n  curator: mim-legacy-to-chebi-migration-v1.0\n  action: Refreshed legacy MediaIngredientMech links to CHEBI keying\n  notes: 'Replaced 37 legacy mediaingredientmech_term link(s) with mediaingredientmech_chebi_term\n    (id-safe: ingredient''s own CHEBI + label). MIM deprecated the MediaIngredientMech:NNNNNN\n    id scheme.'\n- timestamp: '2026-06-08T23:19:36.186877+00:00'\n  curator: chebi-regrounding-v1.0\n  action: Corrected CHEBI ingredient grounding (audit G21/G22)\n  notes: Re-grounded 2 term reference(s) to the correct CHEBI (see reports/chebi_grounding_audit.md).\n    Label-conditional fixes for pyridoxine/pyridoxamine, glycerol, MnSO4, Ca(NO3)2,\n    selenate; casamino acids de-grounded (mixture, no single CHEBI).\n- timestamp: '2026-08-20T19:01:36.836700+00:00'\n  curator: apply_mim_groundings.py\n  action: Adopted MIM published grounding\n  notes: Grounded 5 ingredient(s) from MIM's ingredient_mappings.sssom.tsv (2026-08-18),\n    exactMatch only, where this record carried no CHEBI term (#308).\n- timestamp: '2026-08-21T01:26:30.332195+00:00'\n  curator: chebi-regrounding-v1.0\n  action: Corrected CHEBI ingredient grounding (audit G21/G22/G24)\n  notes: 'Re-grounded 1 term reference(s) to the correct CHEBI (audit G21/G22/G24;\n    see reports/chebi_grounding_audit.md): CHEBI:140435→CHEBI:16113 ×1.'\n- timestamp: '2026-08-25T00:00:00-07:00'\n  curator: fix_mediadb_leading_compounds.py\n  action: RESTORED_CORRUPT_SOURCE_COMPOUND\n  notes: Restored C00002 as ATP (CHEBI:15422) from the MediaDB row sequence; resolves\n    the 2026-08-24 EMPTY_INGREDIENT_NAME review finding.\n- timestamp: '2026-08-31T04:06:11.218057+00:00'\n  curator: repair_mediadb_names.py\n  action: REPAIRED_MEDIADB_TRUNCATED_NAME\n  notes: Restored 1 ingredient name(s) truncated at a parenthesis by the MediaDB SQL\n    parser. Resolved against MEDIADB:33's own compound list in media_database.07Oct2015.sql,\n    requiring a unique prefix match and, where more than one matched, an equal Amount_mM.\n- timestamp: '2026-10-14T00:09:58.559887+00:00'\n  curator: codex\n  action: ADDED_PAPER_CITATIONS_WITH_SCOPED_NOTES\n  notes: Added or enriched bibliographic metadata, archived source/Markdown links,\n    title/group excerpts and qualified NCBI taxonomy notes. Non-operational identity\n    review only; no experimental, formulation, variant, growth or concentration curation.\n    Preserved all original recipe fields, history and reference identifiers.\n  source: PMID:9988320\nmedia_term:\n  preferred_term: MediaDB Medium 33\n  term:\n    id: MEDIADB:33\n    label: CDM/LP\nnotes: 'Source: MediaDB (Chemically-defined media for genome-sequenced organisms)\n  Reference: https://mediadb.systemsbiology.net/'\napplications:\n- Cultivation of genome-sequenced organisms\n- Metabolic modeling\n- Systems biology research\nhigh_metal: true\nreferences:\n- reference: PMID:9988320\n  title: 'Leishmania spp: completely defined medium without serum and macromolecules\n    (CDM/LP) for the continuous in vitro cultivation of infective promastigote forms.'\n  authors: Merlen T; Sereno D; Brajon N; Rostand F; Lemesre JL\n  year: 1999\n  notes: 'source_type=journal_article; discovery_mode=MediaDB_source_cross_reference;\n    accessed_on=2026-10-14; source_access=archived_PubMed_abstract; review_scope=Bibliographic\n    title and taxonomic identity only; archived abstract is not approval of any experiment\n    or formulation.; owner=MEDIADB:33; discovery_sourceID=9; source_url=https://doi.org/10.4269/ajtmh.1999.60.41;\n    alternate_identifier=doi:10.4269/ajtmh.1999.60.41; Historical MediaDB metadata\n    retained for comparison: title=\"Leishmania spp.: completely defined medium without\n    serum and macromolecules (cdm/lp) for the continuous in vitro cultivation of infective\n    promastigote forms \"; first_author=\"Merlen\"; year=1999. Publication identity is\n    separate from historical spelling and dating differences. raw=references_cache/papers/PMID_9988320.xml;\n    markdown=references_cache/papers/PMID_9988320.md; Bibliographic title; exact excerpt=\"Leishmania\n    spp\". Reported organism/group=Leishmania spp; canonical scientific name=Leishmania;\n    NCBITaxon:5658; actual rank=genus; taxonomy_match=genus_level_only_not_named_species_or_subgenus;\n    role=bibliographic-title mention only; no strain, formulation, growth or experimental-outcome\n    assertion. Lookup_on=2026-10-13; https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=taxonomy&id=5658&retmode=xml;\n    taxonomy_archive=references_cache/papers/taxonomy/growth-next-nonoperational-20261013.xml;\n    taxonomy_markdown=references_cache/papers/taxonomy/growth-next-nonoperational-20261013.md.\n    The genus-level title is not narrowed to a species or to the homonymous subgenus.\n    Review is limited to publication identity, title-level organism mentions and taxonomy.\n    Abstract content is archived but not used here to assert experimental findings.\n    This is not an exhaustive abstract or whole-paper organism inventory. The pinned\n    MediaDB source-to-owner join establishes a historical bibliographic lead only,\n    not exact recipe equivalence. Formulation identity, study-specific differences\n    and variant destination remain unassessed in this non-operational citation task.\n    No cultivation conditions, optimization, virulence, growth associations or ingredient\n    amounts are extracted or curated. Correction/retraction coverage is limited to\n    archived metadata. Original ingredients, amounts, preparation, history, evidence\n    and links are preserved, not newly certified. No new native growth assertion,\n    resolved variant or concentration evidence.'\n"
