: Silicone antifoam (BDH)\n  concentration:\n    value: '0.025'\n    unit: ML_PER_L\n  notes: Source-specific silicone antifoam preparation; no single compound identity,\n    density or generic stock strength inferred. Source reports 0.025 mL per liter\n    of medium.\n  evidence:\n  - reference: doi:10.1002/yea.320080703\n    supports: SUPPORT\n    snippet: 0·025 ml silicone antifoam (BDH)\n    explanation: 'Supports the omitted basal-medium antifoam ingredient and the source-specific\n      dose basis for ingredients[21]. add explicit concentration. Basis excerpt: ''on\n      a mineral medium containing per litre:''. Printed page 502; https://repository.tudelft.nl/file/File_025a63db-3c03-4a9d-b18c-d37a795e6cad.\n      No density or final-volume conversion.'\npreparation_steps:\n- step_number: 1\n  action: DISSOLVE\n  description: Prepare the mineral-medium base with the source-specific mineral inputs;\n    add the vitamins separately after heat sterilization.\n- step_number: 2\n  action: ADJUST_PH\n  description: Adjust pH if specified in original formulation\n- step_number: 3\n  action: HEAT\n  description: Heat-sterilize the mineral medium at 120 C before adding the filter-sterilized\n    vitamins. The inspected source passage does not specify hold time or pressure.\n- step_number: 4\n  action: MIX\n  description: Add the filter-sterilized vitamins after heat sterilization, at the\n    source-stated final vitamin concentrations. Filtration pore size and addition\n    temperature are not specified.\ncuration_history:\n- timestamp: '2026-01-27T07:21:46.235325Z'\n  curator: mediadb-import\n  action: Imported from MediaDB\n  notes: 'Source: MediaDB (Institute for Systems Biology), Medium ID: 398, Reference:\n    Mazumdar et al. (2014) PLOS One'\n- timestamp: '2026-01-28T19:48:44.390525Z'\n  curator: chebi-enrichment\n  action: Added CHEBI ontology terms to ingredients\n  notes: Enriched using MicrobeMediaParam and MediaDive chemical mappings\n- timestamp: '2026-02-06T05:10:57.076402Z'\n  curator: invalid-chebi-removal\n  action: Removed 1 invalid CHEBI ID(s)\n  notes: Removed CHEBI IDs with invalid format (7+ digits) from MicrobeMediaParam\n    source data\n- timestamp: '2026-03-13T06:20:14.362882Z'\n  curator: culturemech-id-assigner-v1.0\n  action: Assigned CultureMech ID\n  notes: 'Assigned stable identifier: CultureMech:010556'\n- timestamp: '2026-03-17T17:06:08.000000Z'\n  curator: mediaingredientmech-enrichment-v1.0\n  action: Added MediaIngredientMech links\n  notes: Linked ingredients to MediaIngredientMech identifiers\n- timestamp: '2026-03-17T19:46:33.407543+00:00'\n  curator: normalize_media_names_to_snake_case.py\n  action: NAME_NORMALIZED\n  notes: Normalized name from \"'Yeast Mineral Medium (7.5 g/L Ethanol\" to \"yeast_mineral_medium_7_5_g_l_ethanol\"\n    for consistent matching\n- timestamp: '2026-06-05T07:41:57.308346+00:00'\n  curator: mim-legacy-to-chebi-migration-v1.0\n  action: Refreshed legacy MediaIngredientMech links to CHEBI keying\n  notes: 'Replaced 13 legacy mediaingredientmech_term link(s) with mediaingredientmech_chebi_term\n    (id-safe: ingredient''s own CHEBI + label). MIM deprecated the MediaIngredientMech:NNNNNN\n    id scheme.'\n- timestamp: '2026-06-08T23:19:52.088210+00:00'\n  curator: chebi-regrounding-v1.0\n  action: Corrected CHEBI ingredient grounding (audit G21/G22)\n  notes: Re-grounded 2 term reference(s) to the correct CHEBI (see reports/chebi_grounding_audit.md).\n    Label-conditional fixes for pyridoxine/pyridoxamine, glycerol, MnSO4, Ca(NO3)2,\n    selenate; casamino acids de-grounded (mixture, no single CHEBI).\n- timestamp: '2026-08-31T06:18:33.083161+00:00'\n  curator: repair_mediadb_names.py\n  action: REPAIRED_MEDIADB_TRUNCATED_NAME\n  notes: Restored the medium's own name in media_term.term.label, original_name. The\n    MediaDB SQL parser truncated every value containing a parenthesis at that parenthesis;\n    recovered from media_database.07Oct2015.sql.\n- timestamp: '2026-10-10T05:48:57.196164+00:00'\n  curator: codex\n  action: CURATED_YEAST_MINERAL_SOURCED_INGREDIENTS\n  notes: Reviewed source-specific ingredient changes. Two papers, four formulations;\n    carbon source dose and batch/chemostat stage must not be conflated. Twenty-six\n    mineral amounts have an explicit water-input/final-volume boundary; two molybdate\n    claims have a printed formula conflict. Seven vitamin amounts per record are final\n    concentrations; both papers directly report para-aminobenzoic acid 0.2 mg/L, not\n    the database 0.1458 mM assertion. The omitted silicone antifoam is 0.025 mL per\n    liter of medium in 1992; 0.05 mL per liter water input in 1996. No density or\n    final-volume conversion is inferred. Existing ethanol parent/child notes saying\n    only ethanol differs must be qualified when source antifoam and experimental-stage\n    evidence is applied. Paper-specific benzoate treatments are not a fixed universal\n    basal ingredient dose. DOI identity checked against PubMed; DOI resolver web attempts\n    failed. Downloaded repository PDFs and page images provide the inspected concentration\n    evidence. No automatic reference-validator pass, numeric equivalence of old conversions,\n    exhaustive growth review, or new organism association is asserted.\n  source: doi:10.1002/yea.320080703; https://mediadb.systemsbiology.net/defined_media/media/398/;\n    https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A15940; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A86158;\n    https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A30753; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A86368;\n    https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A53503; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A32312;\n    https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A75213; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A31440;\n    https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A31795; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A75836;\n    doi:10.1002/(SICI)1097-0061(19960315)12:3<247::AID-YEA911>3.0.CO;2-I\n  changes: '{\"added_ingredient\": {\"concentration\": {\"unit\": \"ML_PER_L\", \"value\": \"0.025\"},\n    \"field\": \"ingredients[21]\", \"preferred_term\": \"Silicone antifoam (BDH)\"}, \"evidence_entries_added\":\n    55, \"ingredient_field_changes\": [{\"field\": \"ingredients[0].concentration\", \"new\":\n    {\"unit\": \"MG_PER_L\", \"value\": \"15\"}, \"old\": {\"unit\": \"MILLIMOLAR\", \"value\": \"0.05133\"}},\n    {\"field\": \"ingredients[1].concentration\", \"new\": {\"unit\": \"MG_PER_L\", \"value\":\n    \"0.05\"}, \"old\": {\"unit\": \"MILLIMOLAR\", \"value\": \"0.0002047\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[2].preferred_term\",\n    \"new\": \"nicotinic acid\", \"old\": \"Nicotinate\"}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[2].concentration\",\n    \"new\": {\"unit\": \"MG_PER_L\", \"value\": \"1\"}, \"old\": {\"unit\": \"MILLIMOLAR\", \"value\":\n    \"0.008123\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[3].concentration\", \"new\": {\"unit\": \"MG_PER_L\",\n    \"value\": \"0.1\"}, \"old\": {\"unit\": \"MILLIMOLAR\", \"value\": \"0.0006024\"}}, {\"field\":\n    \"ingredients[4].concentration\", \"new\": {\"unit\": \"G_PER_L\", \"value\": \"7.5\"}, \"old\":\n    {\"unit\": \"MILLIMOLAR\", \"value\": \"162.8\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[5].concentration\",\n    \"new\": {\"unit\": \"MG_PER_L\", \"value\": \"25\"}, \"old\": {\"unit\": \"MILLIMOLAR\", \"value\":\n    \"0.1388\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[6].preferred_term\", \"new\": \"calcium chloride\n    dihydrate\", \"old\": \"Calcium chloride anhydrous\"}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[6].concentration\",\n    \"new\": {\"unit\": \"MG_PER_L\", \"value\": \"4.5\"}, \"old\": {\"unit\": \"MILLIMOLAR\", \"value\":\n    \"0.03061\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[6].term\", \"new\": {\"id\": \"CHEBI:86158\", \"label\":\n    \"calcium chloride dihydrate\"}, \"old\": {\"id\": \"CHEBI:3312\", \"label\": \"calcium dichloride\"}},\n    {\"field\": \"ingredients[7].preferred_term\", \"new\": \"4-aminobenzoic acid\", \"old\":\n    \"4-Aminobenzoate\"}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[7].concentration\"