entry; molecular\n    formula field; matching page title\", \"new\": \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:31795\",\n    \"old\": \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A31795\", \"pointer\": [\"references\",\n    10, \"reference\"], \"snippet\": \"7H2O.Mg.O4S\"}, {\"kind\": \"bibliography_reference_urls_corrected\",\n    \"locator\": \"Official ChEBI entry; molecular formula field; matching page title\",\n    \"new\": \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:75836\", \"old\": \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A75836\",\n    \"pointer\": [\"references\", 11, \"reference\"], \"snippet\": \"Fe.7H2O.O4S\"}]'\nmedia_term:\n  preferred_term: MediaDB Medium 398\n  term:\n    id: MEDIADB:398\n    label: Yeast Mineral Medium (7.5 g/L Ethanol)\nnotes: 'Source: MediaDB (Chemically-defined media for genome-sequenced organisms)\n  Reference: https://mediadb.systemsbiology.net/'\napplications:\n- Cultivation of genome-sequenced organisms\n- Metabolic modeling\n- Systems biology research\nvariant_children:\n- path: data/normalized_yaml/fungal/yeast_mineral_medium_7_9_g_l_ethanol.yaml\n  relationship: CONCENTRATION_VARIANT\n  id: CultureMech:010558\n  name: yeast_mineral_medium_7_9_g_l_ethanol\n  notes: 'Related mineral-media formulations from different primary studies: Verduyn\n    1992 uses 7.5 g/L ethanol in chemostat medium and reports 0.025 mL antifoam per\n    liter medium; Flikweert 1996 uses 7.9 g/L initial ethanol in batch culture and\n    reports 0.05 mL antifoam per liter demineralized-water input. They are not asserted\n    identical except for ethanol; no conversion between water-input and final-medium\n    doses is inferred.'\nreferences:\n- reference: doi:10.1002/yea.320080703\n  title: 'Effect of Benzoic Acid on Metabolic Fluxes in Yeasts: A Continuous-Culture\n    Study on the Regulation of Respiration and Alcoholic Fermentation'\n  notes: 'source_type=journal_article; discovery_mode=existing_database_source_link_then_manual_web_search;\n    accessed_on=2026-10-10; Inspected repository PDF: https://repository.tudelft.nl/file/File_025a63db-3c03-4a9d-b18c-d37a795e6cad;\n    printed page 502; DOI identity verified in PubMed; DOI resolver fetch failed;\n    page image inspected manually. Manual page-image transcription; line-wrap hyphenation\n    joined, chemical subscripts and unit superscripts flattened to ASCII; centered\n    decimal points preserved. OCR is not accepted as a faithful formula transcript.'\n  authors: Cornelis Verduyn; Erik Postma; W. Alexander Scheffers; Johannes P. van\n    Dijken\n  year: 1992\n- reference: https://mediadb.systemsbiology.net/defined_media/media/398/\n  title: 'Media: Yeast mineral medium (7.5 g/l ethanol)'\n  notes: source_type=web_page; discovery_mode=existing_source_capture; accessed_on=2026-10-10;\n    Accession-specific MediaDB HTML table, corroborated against dated 2015-10-07 SQL\n    export; database assertions are not independent primary concentration verification.\n    Publication year and named authors not established.\n- reference: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:15940\n  title: nicotinic acid (CHEBI:15940)\n  notes: source_type=web_page; discovery_mode=pinned_mim_cross_reference_then_official_ontology;\n    accessed_on=2026-10-10; Official ChEBI formula manually inspected; pinned MIM\n    lookup checked separately. Identity evidence only, not a concentration source.\n    No publication year inferred.\n- reference: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:86158\n  title: calcium chloride dihydrate (CHEBI:86158)\n  notes: source_type=web_page; discovery_mode=pinned_mim_cross_reference_then_official_ontology;\n    accessed_on=2026-10-10; Official ChEBI formula manually inspected; pinned MIM\n    lookup checked separately. Identity evidence only, not a concentration source.\n    No publication year inferred.\n- reference: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:30753\n  title: 4-aminobenzoic acid (CHEBI:30753)\n  notes: source_type=web_page; discovery_mode=pinned_mim_cross_reference_then_official_ontology;\n    accessed_on=2026-10-10; Official ChEBI formula manually inspected; pinned MIM\n    lookup checked separately. Identity evidence only, not a concentration source.\n    No publication year inferred.\n- reference: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:86368\n  title: manganese(II) chloride tetrahydrate (CHEBI:86368)\n  notes: source_type=web_page; discovery_mode=pinned_mim_cross_reference_then_official_ontology;\n    accessed_on=2026-10-10; Official ChEBI formula manually inspected; pinned MIM\n    lookup checked separately. Identity evidence only, not a concentration source.\n    No publication year inferred.\n- reference: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:53503\n  title: cobalt chloride hexahydrate (CHEBI:53503)\n  notes: source_type=web_page; discovery_mode=pinned_mim_cross_reference_then_official_ontology;\n    accessed_on=2026-10-10; Official ChEBI formula manually inspected; pinned MIM\n    lookup checked separately. Identity evidence only, not a concentration source.\n    No publication year inferred.\n- reference: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:32312\n  title: zinc sulfate heptahydrate (CHEBI:32312)\n  notes: source_type=web_page; discovery_mode=pinned_mim_cross_reference_then_official_ontology;\n    accessed_on=2026-10-10; Official ChEBI formula manually inspected; pinned MIM\n    lookup checked separately. Identity evidence only, not a concentration source.\n    No publication year inferred.\n- reference: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:75213\n  title: sodium molybdate dihydrate (CHEBI:75213)\n  notes: source_type=web_page; discovery_mode=pinned_mim_cross_reference_then_official_ontology;\n    accessed_on=2026-10-10; Official ChEBI formula manually inspected; pinned MIM\n    lookup checked separately. Identity evidence only, not a concentration source.\n    No publication year inferred.\n- reference: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:31440\n  title: copper(II) sulfate pentahydrate (CHEBI:31440)\n  notes: source_type=web_page; discovery_mode=pinned_mim_cross_reference_then_official_ontology;\n    accessed_on=2026-10-10; Official ChEBI formula manually inspected; pinned MIM\n    lookup checked separately. Identity evidence only, not a concentration source.\n    No publication year inferred.\n- reference: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:31795\n  title: magnesium sulfate heptahydrate (CHEBI:31795)\n  notes: source_type=web_page; discovery_mode=pinned_mim_cross_reference_then_official_ontology;\n    accessed_on=2026-10-10; Official ChEBI formula manually inspected; pinned MIM\n    lookup checked separately. Identity evidence only, not a concentration source.\n    No publication year inferred.\n- reference: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:75836\n  title: iron(2+) sulfate heptahydrate (CHEBI:75836)\n  notes: source_type=web_page; discovery_mode=pinned_mim_cross_reference_then_official_ontology;\n    accessed_on=2026-10-10; Official ChEBI formula manually inspected; pinned MIM\n    lookup checked separately. Identity evidence only, not a concentration source.\n    No publication year inferred.\n- reference: doi:10.1002/(SICI)1097-0061(19960315)12:3<247::AID-YEA911>3.0.CO;2-I\n  title: 'Pyruvate Decarboxylase: An Indispensable Enzyme for Growth of Saccharomyces\n    cerevisiae on Glucose'\n  notes: 'source_type=journal_article; discovery_mode=existing_database_source_link_then_manual_web_search;\n    accessed_on=2026-10-10; Inspected repository PDF: https://repository.tudelft.nl/file/File_980a303e-e5c4-40e9-ae2c-d1efee438339?preview=1;\n    printed page 250; DOI identity verified in PubMed; DOI resolver fetch failed;\n    page image inspected manually. Manual page-image transcription; line-wrap hyphenation\n    joined, chemical subscripts and unit superscripts flattened to ASCII; centered\n    decimal points preserved. OCR is not accepted as a faithful formula transcript.'\n  authors: Marcel T. Flikweert; Linda van der Zanden; Wouter M. Th. M. Janssen; H.\n    Yde Steensma; Johannes P. van Dijken; Jack T. Pronk\n  year: 1996\nevidence:\n- reference: doi:10.1002/yea.320080703\n  supports: SUPPORT\n  snippet: Filter-sterilized vitamins were added after heat sterilization (120°C)\n    of this medium.\n  explanation: 'Supports preparation_steps[0], preparation_steps[2] and preparation_steps[3]:\n    keep vitamin addition after heat sterilization at 120 C. HEAT and MIX do not assert\n    steam pressure, hold time or the FILTER_STERILIZE enum''s 0.22 micrometer pore\n    size. The generic pH-adjustment placeholder is retained, not newly certified.\n    Printed page 502; https://repository.tudelft.nl/file/File_025a63db-3c03-4a9d-b18c-d37a795e6cad\n    Additional exact excerpt: ''0·025 ml silicone antifoam (BDH)''. Supports the qualification\n    of ethanol parent/child formulation descriptions and the source-specific antifoam\n    difference, not an exact-equivalence or merge claim. Separate carbon-dose excerpt:\n    ''7·5 g l-1 ethanol''. Printed page 502; https://repository.tudelft.nl/file/File_025a63db-3c03-4a9d-b18c-d37a795e6cad.\n    carbon source supplied to chemostat medium; not residual culture concentration'\n- reference: doi:10.1002/(SICI)1097-0061(19960315)12:3<247::AID-YEA911>3.0.CO;2-I\n  supports: SUPPORT\n  snippet: silicone antifoam (BDH), 0·05 ml\n  explanation: 'Supports the qualification of ethanol parent/child formulation descriptions\n    and the source-specific antifoam difference, not an exact-equivalence or merge\n    claim. Separate carbon-dose excerpt: ''ethanol (7·9 g l-1 initial concentration)''.\n    Printed page 250; https://repository.tudelft.nl/file/File_980a303e-e5c4-40e9-ae2c-d1efee438339?preview=1.\n    initial batch concentration, not chemostat reservoir concentration'\n"
