        "text": "id: CultureMech:010558\nname: yeast_mineral_medium_7_9_g_l_ethanol\noriginal_name: Yeast Mineral Medium (7.9 g/L Ethanol)\ncategory: fungal\nmedium_type: DEFINED\ncomposition_type: DEFINED\nphysical_state: LIQUID\ningredients:\n- preferred_term: EDTA\n  term:\n    id: CHEBI:4735\n    label: ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid\n  concentration:\n    value: '0.05133'\n    unit: MILLIMOLAR\n  mediaingredientmech_chebi_term:\n    id: CHEBI:4735\n    label: ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid\n  evidence:\n  - reference: https://mediadb.systemsbiology.net/defined_media/media/400/\n    supports: SUPPORT\n    snippet: '0.05133'\n    explanation: 'Historical database provenance for ingredients[0].concentration\n      (EDTA): this accession''s table labels the amount in mM and reports 0.05133\n      mM. This supports what MediaDB asserted, not independent confirmation of the\n      current concentration; primary-source disposition follows separately.'\n  - reference: doi:10.1002/(SICI)1097-0061(19960315)12:3<247::AID-YEA911>3.0.CO;2-I\n    supports: PARTIAL\n    snippet: EDTA, 15 mg\n    explanation: 'Context only for ingredients[0].concentration; retained 0.05133\n      mM is an unverified database assertion. The source gives mass per liter of demineralized-water\n      input, not explicit final solution volume; retain and qualify database molarity,\n      not a certified concentration. Basis excerpt: ''The mineral medium contained\n      per litre of demineralized water:''. printed page 250, PDF page 4; Materials\n      and Methods / Media; Batch cultivation in fermenters for carbon amounts. none;\n      direct source units, no mass/molar or assumed-volume conversion. PDF capture\n      and transcription conventions are identified in the bibliography.'\n  notes: 'Ingredient source review: The source gives mass per liter of demineralized-water\n    input, not explicit final solution volume; retain and qualify database molarity,\n    not a certified concentration. Source amount: 15 mg; input per liter of demineralized\n    water; final solution volume not explicit. Retained 0.05133 mM is a database assertion,\n    not independently verified final concentration.'\n- preferred_term: Biotin\n  term:\n    id: CHEBI:15956\n    label: biotin\n  concentration:\n    value: '0.05'\n    unit: MG_PER_L\n  notes: 'Cross-references: KEGG:btn Imported cross-reference annotation retained\n    as database provenance, not new supplied-form evidence. Ingredient source review:\n    Restore the directly reported source mass concentration; no molecular-weight conversion\n    or claim that every historic conversion was wrong. Source amount: 0.05 mg; final\n    vitamin concentration per liter.'\n  mediaingredientmech_chebi_term:\n    id: CHEBI:15956\n    label: biotin\n  evidence:\n  - reference: https://mediadb.systemsbiology.net/defined_media/media/400/\n    supports: SUPPORT\n    snippet: '0.0002047'\n    explanation: 'Historical database provenance for ingredients[1].concentration\n      (Biotin): this accession''s table labels the amount in mM and reports 0.0002047\n      mM. This supports what MediaDB asserted, not independent confirmation of the\n      current concentration; primary-source disposition follows separately.'\n  - reference: doi:10.1002/(SICI)1097-0061(19960315)12:3<247::AID-YEA911>3.0.CO;2-I\n    supports: SUPPORT\n    snippet: biotin, 0·05 mg\n    explanation: 'Supports ingredients[1].concentration for the supplied ingredient\n      in this exact formulation: 0.05 MG_PER_L. Restore the directly reported source\n      mass concentration; no molecular-weight conversion or claim that every historic\n      conversion was wrong. Basis excerpt: ''to final concentrations per litre of:''.\n      printed page 250, PDF page 4; Materials and Methods / Media; Batch cultivation\n      in fermenters for carbon amounts. none; direct source units, no mass/molar or\n      assumed-volume conversion. PDF capture and transcription conventions are identified\n      in the bibliography.'\n- preferred_term: nicotinic acid\n  concentration:\n    value: '1.0'\n    unit: MG_PER_L\n  notes: 'Cross-references: KEGG:nac Imported cross-reference annotation retained\n    as database provenance, not new supplied-form evidence. Ingredient source review:\n    Restore the directly reported source mass concentration; no molecular-weight conversion\n    or claim that every historic conversion was wrong. Source amount: 1.0 mg; final\n    vitamin concentration per liter.'\n  term:\n    id: CHEBI:15940\n    label: nicotinic acid\n  evidence:\n  - reference: https://mediadb.systemsbiology.net/defined_media/media/400/\n    supports: SUPPORT\n    snippet: '0.008123'\n    explanation: 'Historical database provenance for ingredients[2].concentration\n      (Nicotinate): this accession''s table labels the amount in mM and reports 0.008123\n      mM. This supports what MediaDB asserted, not independent confirmation of the\n      current concentration; primary-source disposition follows separately.'\n  - reference: doi:10.1002/(SICI)1097-0061(19960315)12:3<247::AID-YEA911>3.0.CO;2-I\n    supports: SUPPORT\n    snippet: nicotinic acid, 1·0 mg\n    explanation: 'Supports ingredients[2].concentration for the supplied ingredient\n      in this exact formulation: 1.0 MG_PER_L. Restore the directly reported source\n      mass concentration; no molecular-weight conversion or claim that every historic\n      conversion was wrong. Basis excerpt: ''to final concentrations per litre of:''.\n      printed page 250, PDF page 4; Materials and Methods / Media; Batch cultivation\n      in fermenters for carbon amounts. none; direct source units, no mass/molar or\n      assumed-volume conversion. PDF capture and transcription conventions are identified\n      in the bibliography.'\n  - reference: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:15940\n    supports: SUPPORT\n    snippet: C6H5NO2\n    explanation: 'Identity review for ingredients[2] (Nicotinate): Suppl