atch cultivation\n      in fermenters for carbon amounts. none; direct source units, no mass/molar or\n      assumed-volume conversion. PDF capture and transcription conventions are identified\n      in the bibliography.'\n  notes: 'Ingredient source review: Restore the directly reported source mass concentration;\n    no molecular-weight conversion or claim that every historic conversion was wrong.\n    Source amount: 1.0 mg; final vitamin concentration per liter.'\n- preferred_term: Potassium dihydrogen phosphate\n  concentration:\n    value: '22.04'\n    unit: MILLIMOLAR\n  term:\n    id: CHEBI:63036\n    label: potassium dihydrogen phosphate\n  evidence:\n  - reference: https://mediadb.systemsbiology.net/defined_media/media/400/\n    supports: SUPPORT\n    snippet: '22.04'\n    explanation: 'Historical database provenance for ingredients[20].concentration\n      (Potassium dihydrogen phosphate): this accession''s table labels the amount\n      in mM and reports 22.04 mM. This supports what MediaDB asserted, not independent\n      confirmation of the current concentration; primary-source disposition follows\n      separately.'\n  - reference: doi:10.1002/(SICI)1097-0061(19960315)12:3<247::AID-YEA911>3.0.CO;2-I\n    supports: PARTIAL\n    snippet: KH2PO4, 3 g\n    explanation: 'Context only for ingredients[20].concentration; retained 22.04 mM\n      is an unverified database assertion. The source gives mass per liter of demineralized-water\n      input, not explicit final solution volume; retain and qualify database molarity,\n      not a certified concentration. Basis excerpt: ''The mineral medium contained\n      per litre of demineralized water:''. printed page 250, PDF page 4; Materials\n      and Methods / Media; Batch cultivation in fermenters for carbon amounts. none;\n      direct source units, no mass/molar or assumed-volume conversion. PDF capture\n      and transcription conventions are identified in the bibliography.'\n  notes: 'Ingredient source review: The source gives mass per liter of demineralized-water\n    input, not explicit final solution volume; retain and qualify database molarity,\n    not a certified concentration. Source amount: 3 g; input per liter of demineralized\n    water; final solution volume not explicit. Retained 22.04 mM is a database assertion,\n    not independently verified final concentration.'\n- preferred_term: Silicone antifoam (BDH)\n  notes: Source-specific silicone antifoam preparation; no single compound identity,\n    density or generic stock strength inferred. Source reports 0.05 mL per liter of\n    demineralized-water input; final-medium concentration is not asserted.\n  evidence:\n  - reference: doi:10.1002/(SICI)1097-0061(19960315)12:3<247::AID-YEA911>3.0.CO;2-I\n    supports: SUPPORT\n    snippet: silicone antifoam (BDH), 0·05 ml\n    explanation: 'Supports the omitted basal-medium antifoam ingredient and the source-specific\n      dose basis for ingredients[21]. add unquantified ingredient with 0.05 mL per\n      1 L water input in notes; do not assert final-medium dose. Basis excerpt: ''The\n      mineral medium contained per litre of demineralized water:''. Printed page 250;\n      https://repository.tudelft.nl/file/File_980a303e-e5c4-40e9-ae2c-d1efee438339?preview=1.\n      No density or final-volume conversion.'\npreparation_steps:\n- step_number: 1\n  action: DISSOLVE\n  description: Prepare the mineral-medium base with the source-specific mineral inputs;\n    add the vitamins separately after heat sterilization.\n- step_number: 2\n  action: ADJUST_PH\n  description: Adjust pH if specified in original formulation\n- step_number: 3\n  action: HEAT\n  description: Heat-sterilize the mineral medium at 120 C before adding the filter-sterilized\n    vitamins. The inspected source passage does not specify hold time or pressure.\n- step_number: 4\n  action: MIX\n  description: Add the filter-sterilized vitamins after heat sterilization, at the\n    source-stated final vitamin concentrations. Filtration pore size and addition\n    temperature are not specified.\ncuration_history:\n- timestamp: '2026-01-27T07:21:46.256945Z'\n  curator: mediadb-import\n  action: Imported from MediaDB\n  notes: 'Source: MediaDB (Institute for Systems Biology), Medium ID: 400, Reference:\n    Mazumdar et al. (2014) PLOS One'\n- timestamp: '2026-01-28T19:48:44.326052Z'\n  curator: chebi-enrichment\n  action: Added CHEBI ontology terms to ingredients\n  notes: Enriched using MicrobeMediaParam and MediaDive chemical mappings\n- timestamp: '2026-02-06T05:10:57.014329Z'\n  curator: invalid-chebi-removal\n  action: Removed 1 invalid CHEBI ID(s)\n  notes: Removed CHEBI IDs with invalid format (7+ digits) from MicrobeMediaParam\n    source data\n- timestamp: '2026-03-13T06:20:14.382860Z'\n  curator: culturemech-id-assigner-v1.0\n  action: Assigned CultureMech ID\n  notes: 'Assigned stable identifier: CultureMech:010558'\n- timestamp: '2026-03-17T17:06:08.000000Z'\n  curator: mediaingredientmech-enrichment-v1.0\n  action: Added MediaIngredientMech links\n  notes: Linked ingredients to MediaIngredientMech identifiers\n- timestamp: '2026-03-17T19:46:33.429328+00:00'\n  curator: normalize_media_names_to_snake_case.py\n  action: NAME_NORMALIZED\n  notes: Normalized name from \"'Yeast Mineral Medium (7.9 g/L Ethanol\" to \"yeast_mineral_medium_7_9_g_l_ethanol\"\n    for consistent matching\n- timestamp: '2026-06-05T07:41:57.321555+00:00'\n  curator: mim-legacy-to-chebi-migration-v1.0\n  action: Refreshed legacy MediaIngredientMech links to CHEBI keying\n  notes: 'Replaced 13 legacy mediaingredientmech_term link(s) with mediaingredientmech_chebi_term\n    (id-safe: ingredient''s own CHEBI + label). MIM deprecated the MediaIngredientMech:NNNNNN\n    id scheme.'\n- timestamp: '2026-06-08T23:19:52.101221+00:00'\n  curator: chebi-regrounding-v1.0\n  action: Corrected CHEBI ingredient grounding (audit G21/G22)\n  notes: Re-grounded 2 term reference(s) to the correct CHEBI (see reports/chebi_grounding_audit.md).\n    Label-conditional fixes for pyridoxine/pyridoxamine, glycerol, MnSO4, Ca(NO3)2,\n    selenate; casamino acids de-grounded (mixture, no single CHEBI).\n- timestamp: '2026-08-31T06:18:33.098163+00:00'\n  curator: repair_mediadb_names.py\n  action: REPAIRED_MEDIADB_TRUNCATED_NAME\n  notes: Restored the medium's own name in media_term.term.label, original_name. The\n    MediaDB SQL parser truncated every value containing a parenthesis at that parenthesis;\n    recovered from media_database.07Oct2015.sql.\n- timestamp: '2026-10-10T05:48:57.196164+00:00'\n  curator: codex\n  action: CURATED_YEAST_MINERAL_SOURCED_INGREDIENTS\n  notes: Reviewed source-specific ingredient changes. Two papers, four formulations;\n    carbon source dose and batch/chemostat stage must not be conflated. Twenty-six\n    mineral amounts have an explicit water-input/final-volume boundary; two molybdate\n    claims have a printed formula conflict. Seven vitamin amounts per record are final\n    concentrations; both papers directly report para-aminobenzoic acid 0.2 mg/L, not\n    the database 0.1458 mM assertion. The omitted silicone antifoam is 0.025 mL per\n    liter of medium in 1992; 0.05 mL per liter water input in 1996. No density or\n    final-volume conversion is inferred. Existing ethanol parent/child notes saying\n    only ethanol differs must be qualified when source antifoam and experimental-stage\n    evidence is applied. Paper-specific benzoate treatments are not a fixed universal\n    basal ingredient dose. DOI identity checked against PubMed; DOI resolver web attempts\n    failed. Downloaded repository PDFs and page images provide the inspected concentration\n    evidence. No automatic reference-validator pass, numeric equivalence of old conversions,\n    exhaustive growth review, or new organism association is asserted.\n  source: doi:10.1002/(SICI)1097-0061(19960315)12:3<247::AID-YEA911>3.0.CO;2-I; https://mediadb.systemsbiology.net/defined_media/media/400/;\n    https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A15940; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A86158;\n    https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A30753; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A86368;\n    https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A53503; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A32312;\n    https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A75213; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A31440;\n    https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A31795; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A75836;\n    doi:10.1002/yea.320080703\n  changes: '{\"added_ingredient\": {\"concentration\": null, \"field\": \"ingredients[21]\",\n    \"preferred_term\": \"Silicone antifoam (BDH)\"}, \"evidence_entries_added\": 55, \"ingredient_field_changes\":\n    [{\"field\": \"ingredients[1].concentration\", \"new\": {\"unit\": \"MG_PER_L\", \"value\":\n    \"0.05\"}, \"old\": {\"unit\": \"MILLIMOLAR\", \"value\": \"0.0002047\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[2].preferred_term\",\n    \"new\": \"nicotinic acid\", \"old\": \"Nicotinate\"}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[2].concentration\",\n    \"new\": {\"unit\": \"MG_PER_L\", \"value\": \"1.0\"}, \"old\": {\"unit\": \"MILLIMOLAR\", \"value\":\n    \"0.008123\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[4].concentration\", \"new\": {\"unit\": \"G_PER_L\",\n    \"value\": \"7.9\"}, \"old\": {\"unit\": \"MILLIMOLAR\", \"value\": \"171.5\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[5].concentration\",\n    \"new\": {\"unit\": \"MG_PER_L\", \"value\": \"25.0\"}, \"old\": {\"unit\": \"MILLIMOLAR\", \"value\":\n    \"0.1388\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[6].preferred_term\", \"new\": \"calcium chloride\n    dihydrate\", \"old\": \"Calcium chloride anhydrous\"}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[6].term\",\n    \"new\": {\"id\": \"CHEBI:86158\", \"label\": \"calcium chloride dihydrate\"}, \"old\": {\"id\":\n    \"CHEBI:3312\", \"label\": \"calcium dichloride\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[7].preferred_term\",\n    \"new\": \"4-aminobenzoic acid\", \"old\": \"4-Aminobenzoate\"}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[7].concentration\",\n    \"new\": {\"unit\": \"MG_PER_L\", \"value\": \"0.2\"}, \"old\": {\"unit\": \"MILLIMOLAR\", \"value\":\n    \"0.1458\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[7].term\", \"new\": {\"id\": \"CHEBI:30753\", \"label\":\n    \"4-aminobenzoic acid\"}, \"old\": {\"id\": \"CHEBI:17836\", \"label\": \"4-aminobenzoate\"}},\n    {\"field\": \"ingredients[7].mediaingredientmech_chebi_term\", \"new\": {\"id\": \"CHEBI:30753\",\n    \"label\": \"4-aminobenzoic acid\"}, \"old\": {\"id\": \"CHEBI:17836\", \"label\": \"4-aminobenzoate\"}},\n    {\"field\": \"ingredients[9].concentration\", \"new\": {\"unit\": \"MG_PER_L\", \"value\":\n    \"1.0\"}, \"old\": {\"unit\": \"MILLIMOLAR\", \"value\": \"0.002099\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[10].concentration\",\n    \"new\": {\"unit\": \"MG_PER_L\", \"value\": \"1.0\"}, \"old\": {\"unit\": \"MILLIMOLAR\", \"value\":\n    \"0.004863\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[11].preferred_term\", \"new\": \"manganese(II)\n    chloride tetrahydrate\", \"old\": \"Manganese chloride\"}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[11].term\",\n    \"new\": {\"id\": \"CHEBI:86368\", \"label\": \"manganese(II) chloride tetrahydrate\"},\n    \"old\": {\"id\": \"CHEBI:63041\", \"label\": \"manganese(II) chloride\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[13].preferred_term\",\n    \"new\": \"cobalt chloride hexahydrate\", \"old\": \"Cobalt chloride\"}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[13].term\",\n    \"new\": {\"id\": \"CHEBI:53503\", \"label\": \"cobalt chloride hexahydrate\"}, \"old\": {\"id\":\n    \"CHEBI:35696\", \"label\": \"cobalt dichloride\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[14].preferred_term\",\n    \"new\": \"zinc sulfate heptahydrate\", \"old\": \"Zinc sulfate\"}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[14].term\",\n    \"new\": {\"id\": \"CHEBI:32312\", \"label\": \"zinc sulfate heptahydrate\"}, \"old\": {\"id\":\n    \"CHEBI:35176\", \"label\": \"zinc sulfate\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[14].mediaingredientmech_chebi_term\",\n    \"new\": {\"id\": \"CHEBI:32312\", \"label\": \"zinc sulfate heptahydrate\"}, \"old\": {\"id\":\n    \"CHEBI:35176\", \"label\": \"zinc sulfate\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[15].preferred_term\",\n    \"new\": \"sodium molybdate dihydrate\", \"old\": \"Sodium molybdate\"}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[15].term\",\n    \"new\": {\"id\": \"CHEBI:75213\", \"label\": \"sodium molybdate dihydrate\"}, \"old\": {\"id\":\n    \"CHEBI:75215\", \"label\": \"sodium molybdate (anhydrous)\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[16].preferred_term\",\n    \"new\": \"copper(II) sulfate pentahydrate\", \"old\": \"Cupric sulfate\"}, {\"field\":\n    \"ingredients[16].term\", \"new\": {\"id\": \"CHEBI:31440\", \"label\": \"copper(II) sulfate\n    pentahydrate\"}, \"old\": {\"id\": \"CHEBI:23414\", \"label\": \"copper(II) sulfate\"}},\n    {\"field\": \"ingredients[17].preferred_term\", \"new\": \"magnesium sulfate heptahydrate\",\n    \"old\": \"Magnesium sulfate\"}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[17].term\", \"new\": {\"id\": \"CHEBI:31795\",\n    \"label\": \"magnesium sulfate heptahydrate\"}, \"old\": {\"id\": \"CHEBI:32599\", \"label\":\n    \"magnesium sulfate\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[17].mediaingredientmech_chebi_term\",\n    \"new\": {\"id\": \"CHEBI:31795\", \"label\": \"magnesium sulfate heptahydrate\"}, \"old\":\n    {\"id\": \"CHEBI:32599\", \"label\": \"magnesium sulfate\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[18].preferred_term\",\n    \"new\": \"iron(2+) sulfate heptahydrate\", \"old\": \"Ferrous sulfate\"}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[18].term\",\n    \"new\": {\"id\": \"CHEBI:75836\", \"label\": \"iron(2+) sulfate heptahydrate\"}, \"old\":\n    {\"id\": \"CHEBI:75832\", \"label\": \"iron(2+) sulfate (anhydrous)\"}}, {\"field\": \"ingredients[19].concentration\",\n    \"new\": {\"unit\": \"MG_PER_L\", \"value\": \"1.0\"}, \"old\": {\"unit\": \"MILLIMOLAR\", \"value\":\n    \"0.002965\"}}], \"ingredient_notes\": \"Qualify each original ingredient amount and\n    source basis; preserve imported cross-references as historical database annotations.\",\n    \"preparation_steps\": {\"after\": [{\"action\": \"DISSOLVE\", \"description\": \"Prepare\n    the mineral-medium base with the source-specific mineral inputs; add the vitamins\n    separately after heat sterilization.\", \"step_number\": 1}, {\"action\": \"ADJUST_PH\",\n    \"description\": \"Adjust pH if specified in original formulation\", \"step_number\":\n    2}, {\"action\": \"HEAT\", \"description\": \"Heat-sterilize the mineral medium at 120\n    C before adding the filter-sterilized vitamins. The inspected source passage does\n    not specify hold time or pressure.\", \"step_number\": 3}, {\"action\": \"MIX\", \"description\":\n    \"Add the filter-sterilized vitamins after heat sterilization, at the source-stated\n    final vitamin concentrations. Filtration pore size and addition temperature are\n    not specified.\", \"step_number\": 4}], \"before\": [{\"action\": \"DISSOLVE\", \"description\":\n    \"Dissolve all ingredients in distilled water to specified concentrations\", \"step_number\":\n    1}, {\"action\": \"ADJUST_PH\", \"description\": \"Adjust pH if specified in original\n    formulation\", \"step_number\": 2}, {\"action\": \"FILTER_STERILIZE\", \"description\":\n    \"Sterilize by filtration (0.22 \\u03bcm) to preserve heat-sensitive components\",\n    \"step_number\": 3}]}, \"references_added\": [\"doi:10.1002/(SICI)1097-0061(19960315)12:3<247::AID-YEA911>3.0.CO;2-I\",\n    \"https://mediadb.systemsbiology.net/defined_media/media/400/\", \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A15940\",\n    \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A86158\", \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A30753\",\n    \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A86368\", \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A53503\",\n    \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A32312\", \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A75213\",\n    \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A31440\", \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A31795\",\n    \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A75836\", \"doi:10.1002/yea.320080703\"], \"relationship_descriptions\":\n    {\"parent_media\": {\"after\": {\"id\": \"CultureMech:010556\", \"name\": \"yeast_mineral_medium_7_5_g_l_ethanol\",\n    \"notes\": \"Related mineral-media formulations from different primary studies: Verduyn\n    1992 uses 7.5 g/L ethanol in chemostat medium and reports 0.025 mL antifoam per\n    liter medium; Flikweert 1996 uses 7.9 g/L initial ethanol in batch culture and\n    reports 0.05 mL antifoam per liter demineralized-water input. They are not asserted\n    identical except for ethanol; no conversion between water-input and final-medium\n    doses is inferred.\", \"path\": \"data/normalized_yaml/fungal/yeast_mineral_medium_7_5_g_l_ethanol.yaml\",\n    \"relationship\": \"CONCENTRATION_VARIANT\"}, \"before\": {\"id\": \"CultureMech:010556\",\n    \"name\": \"yeast_mineral_medium_7_5_g_l_ethanol\", \"notes\": \"Reviewed MediaDB yeast\n    mineral ethanol pair; records differ only in ethanol concentration.\", \"path\":\n    \"data/normalized_yaml/fungal/yeast_mineral_medium_7_5_g_l_ethanol.yaml\", \"relationship\":\n    \"CONCENTRATION_VARIANT\"}}, \"variant_modifications\": {\"after\": [\"Related mineral-media\n    formulations from different primary studies: Verduyn 1992 uses 7.5 g/L ethanol\n    in chemostat medium and reports 0.025 mL antifoam per liter medium; Flikweert\n    1996 uses 7.9 g/L initial ethanol in batch culture and reports 0.05 mL antifoam\n    per liter demineralized-water input. They are not asserted identical except for\n    ethanol; no conversion between water-input and final-medium doses is inferred.\"],\n    \"before\": [\"Ethanol increased from 162.8 mM to 171.5 mM while the yeast mineral\n    medium formulation remains unchanged.\"]}}}'\n- timestamp: '2026-10-10T06:24:13+00:00'\n  curator: codex\n  action: CORRECTED_CHEBI_REFERENCE_URL_ENCODING\n  notes: Encoded-colon paths returned HTTP 404; canonical colon paths returned HTTP\n    200. Official page titles and molecular-formula snip